Confirmed the process-substitution failure empirically before writing
it down: diff3 on <(git show ...) reported the entire "ours" stage as
changed and the other two as empty, while the same three stages
extracted to real temp files produced the expected one-region diff.
That is why the skill spends a clause on it — the wrong form fails
silently rather than erroring, which is the dangerous kind.

Dropped the old "most resolution mistakes come from skipping the base"
line. The sentiment is right but the quantifier was unprovable; the
replacement keeps the point — weigh each side against the base, via
both its diff and its commit message — without the false precision.

Left `git checkout --conflict=zdiff3 file` duplicated in section 2 and
section 3a. Different framings (inspect vs. hand-edit) and the skill
already cross-references, so deduping felt like more indirection than
it is worth. Easy to revisit if it drifts.

